# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Mission Control — environment
#
# Nothing here is required to run the dashboard. With an empty .env the app
# boots on PGlite with seeded data and every agent runs in simulate mode.
# Fill these in as you unlock capability; see SETUP_TODO.md for what each one
# actually unblocks.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Storage -----------------------------------------------------------------
# Unset  -> local PGlite database at ./data/mission-control  (default, zero setup)
# Set    -> any Postgres (Supabase / Neon / self-hosted). Same migrations.
#           Use the Session pooler string from Supabase, not db.<ref>.supabase.co.
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://user:pass@host:5432/postgres

# --- Agent runtime -----------------------------------------------------------
# Unset -> every agent runs in simulate mode: real activity + memory rows are
#          written and the tree updates, but no model is called.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# Hard ceiling on what a single agent run may cost, in USD. Runs that would
# exceed it stop and post a blocker instead.
AGENT_MAX_COST_USD=0.50

# --- Chat channel (§6) -------------------------------------------------------
# TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=
# TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID=
# TELEGRAM_WEBHOOK_SECRET=

# --- Scheduler (§7) ----------------------------------------------------------
# Unset -> /api/tick returns 503 and the cadence table never fires on its own.
#          `npm run tick` still works and is unaffected.
# Set    -> /api/tick runs whatever is due. Vercel Cron sends this as a bearer
#          token automatically; any other scheduler sends x-cron-secret.
#          Generate one with:  openssl rand -hex 32
# CRON_SECRET=

# Voice notes. Anthropic has no speech-to-text endpoint, so this is the one
# place another provider is called. Unset -> voice notes reply that they could
# not be transcribed; typed commands are unaffected.
# OPENAI_API_KEY=

# --- Integrations (§8) -------------------------------------------------------
# All optional. An agent whose source is missing reports
# "kaynak kullanilamiyor" rather than inventing a number.
# Month-to-date revenue in the LEDGER and the brief. Tag each charge with
# metadata.branch = web | automation, or the amount is reported as untagged
# rather than guessed into a branch — the two branches keep separate P&Ls.
# STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=

# Lead source for Prospector. Phone numbers cost mobile credits on top of the
# seat price, so the list is capped by credits, not by the agent's KPI.
# APOLLO_API_KEY=

# Cold email. Nothing is ever sent unattended — outreach_send is gated
# unconditionally, so every message waits for an approval on the phone first.
# RESEND_API_KEY=

# Today's calls in the brief. A secret-address .ics feed — in Google Calendar:
# Settings → your calendar → "Secret address in iCal format". No OAuth needed.
# CALENDAR_URL=

# Lighthouse runs through Google PageSpeed Insights. It works without a key at
# low volume; the shared keyless quota runs out fast, and a 429 makes the
# auditor report "could not measure" rather than guess.
# Free key: https://developers.google.com/speed/docs/insights/v5/get-started
# GOOGLE_PAGESPEED_API_KEY=
